tgies/klattsch @ 63dc2c6 (MIT), vendored with patches:
  src/engine/sequencer.js: [TR=ms] sets the formant transition into steady phonemes (default 35 ms, at most 40% of the phoneme; with TR, up to 90%)
  src/engine/sequencer.js: [AV=x] scales loudness (the synth's gain, default 3.5) and glides with the phoneme's transition
  src/engine/sequencer.js: a stop's bank entry may set burstMs (default 25 ms for all)
  src/engine/synth-core.js: shaped, per-parameter transitions: a schedule event may carry curve (1 raised cosine, 2 ease-out) and params
    (the parameters it moves; the others keep their own transitions); a schedule without either renders through the original code
  src/engine/sequencer.js: [TC=n] gives every event that curve; [CO=x] coarticulation: formants move in their own events, a vowel starts at
    and ends toward each neighbouring consonant's locus-equation value F + x (k F + c - F) ([COR=x] at VC; [COCV=ms], [COVC=ms]; [TCF=n]
    the formant events' curve), from bank fields vowel, locus {F1..F3: [k, c]}, locusVC, locusBurst (a stop's burst at the vowel's onset
    formants), transparent (HH: the next vowel's formants), smooth (liquids: no step); under [CO] formant events never go back in
    time and the schedule is sorted by time (stably); without [CO]/[TC] the schedule is unchanged
  src/engine/dsp.js, src/engine/synth-core.js: [GS=1] an LF (Liljencrants-Fant) voice source instead of the Rosenberg pulse: lfShape(Rd) (Fant 1995), [RD=x] [RDE=oct/effort] shape and its effort coupling, [TL=dB at 3 kHz] one-pole tilt, [JIT=%] [SHIM=%] local jitter (closure-to-closure periods) and shimmer, [AM=0..1] noise scaled by the glottal flow while voiced, [FL=x] flutter (Klatt & Klatt 1990), [NT=dB] [AT=dB] one-pole low-pass of the frication / aspiration noise (Klatt's soft low-pass noise); without GS (or GS=0) every sample is as before
  src/engine/dsp.js, src/engine/synth-core.js, src/engine/sequencer.js: [NAS=x] nasals. The synth gains Klatt's (1980) nasal path:
    a resonator FNP/BNP and an antiresonator FNZ/BNZ (each unity gain at 0 Hz, cancelling at FNP = FNZ, BNP = BNZ), a second pair
    FNP2/BNP2, FNZ2/BNZ2, in cascade before the parallel formants, AN, a parallel nasal formant at FNP, and GN, a gain on the whole
    output while the path runs; it runs only once a target carries one of these keys (until then every sample is as before), the
    nasal parameters glide on their own clock, and an event { nasalOnly: true } moves them alone (it is neither a voice-source event
    nor a move of the other parameters, in both the linear and the shaped mode). Under [NAS=x] a bank entry's nasal fields
    (nasal: true, FNP ... BNZ2, AN, GN; nasalizes {...}) are its murmur, every other phoneme's first event and every silence carry
    neutral ones, and a vowel-like neighbour of a nasal (voicing >= 1, not a stop; no pause between) is nasalized over [NASVC]
    (before it, default 0.8) / [NASCV] (after it, 0.5) of its slot, each span at most [NASMS=ms] (absent: no cap), at strength x
    (nasalOnly events toward AN 0.4 at FNP 250, the pairs neutral, GN 1, or the nasal's nasalizes {...}); the pole/zero frequencies
    follow the formant scale; [NAST=ms] times the first event into a nasal and into the (non-stop) phoneme after it; a bare [NAS]
    puts neutral values back. Without [NAS] bank nasal fields are dropped and the schedule is unchanged (audio fixture:
    klattsing/test/audio.test.js)
  src/engine/sequencer.js: a stop's bank entry may set closure ({fields, inMs, fade}: what sounds while the tract is closed instead of
    silence, e.g. a voice bar: the parameters it sets reached in inMs (default 20, at most 40% of the closure), its A1-A3 times fade by the
    release; under [CO] the formants it sets in a formant event, the others at the vowel's VC boundary) and release: false (no burst, the
    closure fills the slot: an unreleased stop); klattsing's "stops" option generates such entries. An entry without them renders as before
  src/engine/synth-core.js, src/engine/sequencer.js: [FRIC=x] fricatives. The synth gains a frication path after Klatt's (1980)
    parallel branch: white noise (under [GS] with AM, while voiced, modulated by the glottal flow like the source's own noise, at
    depth AM x voicing x FM; FM default 1) through three resonators of its own, FF1/BF1/AF1, FF2/BF2/AF2, FF3/BF3/AF3 (bandpass
    biquads, the middle one's sign flipped), and AB, a bypass, added to the formant output; each parameter glides linearly on its
    own clock, and { fricOnly: true } events move them alone. It runs only
    once a target carries one of these keys (until then every sample is as before). Under [FRIC=x] a bank entry's frication
    {FF1 ... AB, FM, rise, fall, fallTo, fallToC, in} drives it in fricOnly events (frequencies and FM at the phoneme's start, amplitudes
    times x over rise ms, falling over the last fall share of the slot to fallTo before a vowel-like phoneme or fallToC before
    anything else but another fricative, which takes over without a fall), in (ms) times the entry's first main-path event (it
    also wins over [NAST] after a nasal), every other phoneme's first event and every silence zero the amplitudes (also the
    first one after a bare [FRIC]), and such an entry is never nasalized ([NAS]); the frequencies follow the formant scale. A
    frication field removed from an entry (null) keeps the previous fricative's value. Without [FRIC] the
    frication fields are dropped and the schedule is unchanged (audio fixture: klattsing/test/audio.test.js, round 3's BASE
    included); klattsing's "fricatives" option generates the entries
